        "html": "<h1>Application platform health and rollout acceptance</h1>\n<p>BlueTusk’s three Clean Architecture reference applications are production-shaped\nworkloads, but Kubernetes desired state is not proof that a workload is actually\nrunning. A stale Pod object can continue to show <code>Running</code> and a stale EndpointSlice\ncan continue to show <code>ready: true</code> after a kubelet or datastore has stopped\nreconciling that object. Application rollout acceptance therefore uses independent\ncontrol-plane, node-runtime, storage, database and workload checks.</p>\n<p>This gate is required before either reference application can begin a formal V1\npilot. It is read-only: it does not restart nodes, delete Pods, repair volumes,\nchange Secrets, or deploy images.</p>\n<h2>Commands</h2>\n<p>Run the infrastructure preflight before rendering or applying an RC release:</p>\n"
